 in cassettes E F   Labeled  left axilla contents  lower sampling  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibroadipose tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and representative sections are submitted  Labeled  left axilla contents  hilar nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm yellow tan soft tissue specimen  Lymph nodes are dissected and representative sections are submitted  Section code  A  Tumor B  Tumor superior C  Tumor inferior D  Tumor deep E F  Parenchyma away from tumor  suspicious cystic areas G H  Left axilla contents  lower nodes I K  Left axilla contents  higher nodes Resident  TAN A  INCE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   LOWER   PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   HIGHER     report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  John H Eichhorn  M D  Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Prior right breast cancer  new left breast calcifications  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION  MICRO INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  A FEW CELLS AND CELL CLUSTERS ON 2 OF 9 BLOCKS  SPANNING LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM  AND LOCATED LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INFERIOR MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  WITH COMEDONECROSIS  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  SCATTERED SMALL FOCI ON 8 OF 9 BLOCKS  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  AND EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR  SUPERIOR AND INFERIOR MARGINS  NOTE  By immunoperoxidase methods  a few isolated cytokeratin positive tumor cells within desmoplastic stroma are not surrounded by cells that are stainable for myoepithelial markers  p63  calponin  heavy chain myosin   confirming their invasive nature  No lymphovascular invasion is identified  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  The very small number of invasive tumor cells that might be available for evaluation  however  may limit these results  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan yellow to red  lobulated  oriented  irregular piece of fibrofatty breast tissue with a short suture designating the superior margin  and a long suture designating the lateral margin  A localization wire is received in the bag detached from the specimen  The long axis is medial to lateral  and the specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis from the lateral to medial margin to reveal a grossly unremarkable pr enchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  from lateral to medial with an en face section of the lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and an en face section of the medial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells show moderate  2   to strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  The sections stained for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins and HER 2 c erbB 2 show only a few invasive tumors  insufficient for evaluation of staining of tumor cells  Dr  John Eichhorn has also reviewed these slides and concurs with this interpretation  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained