 specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a stellate scar  a necrotic mass and a calcified nodule  The tan white stellate fibrotic scar in the outer quadrant  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  lies approximately between 9 and 10 o clock position   0 1cm from the posterior inked margin and 0 3cm from overlying skin  Adjacent and abutting the stellate scar there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm tan yellow ill defined  necrotic mass which grossly abuts the nodule on the overlying skin and lies 2 5cm from posterior inked margin  Approximately 0 8cm medial to the scar in the lower quadrant  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan white fairly well circumscribed calcified nodule which lies 4cm from the posterior inked margin and 3 5cm from overlying skin  The breast parenchyma between the 2 nodules is dense white  rubbery and fibrous  The remaining breast parenchyma contains diffusely tan white rubbery nodular fibrous tissue interspersed with a moderate amount of tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No additional discrete masses or lesions are noted  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are gross appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic scar to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic scar to include adjacent necrotic mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Necrotic mass to overlying skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Calcified nodule to include closest posterior inked margin submitted following decalcification   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma  between the necrotic mass and the calcified nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma  central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous breast parenchyma  inner quadrant  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  Final Diagnosis by Ele