Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 29 CLINICAL DATA  None entered                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 0     GRADE REMOVED_DATE  TWO MICROSCOPIC FOCI  REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIMENSION  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  99 0     COMEDO AND FOCALLY MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  PRESENT IN REMOVED_DATE BLOCKS  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4  PAPILLOMA  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  FIBROSIS  CYSTS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  ADENOSIS  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma arises in intimate association with the ductal carcinoma in situ  No blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is present  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   A few in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma cells  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 27    REVISED REMOVED_DATE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of breast tissue with localizing needle in place and an x ray film  Sectioning reveals a 1 x 1 x 0 6cm slightly firm  comedo type lesion near the needle which approaches to within 0 2cm of the inked margin  A section of the lesion is frozen as FX  1 and submitted in A  The rest of the area corresponding to the calcification is submitted in B through E  The remainder is submitted in F through K  Dr  Ackroyd has retained the radiograph  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  DCIS  HIGH GRADE  COMEDO CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , Unchecked.
