D TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue oriented with a short suture indicating superior margin and a long suture designating lateral margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular shaped  white  firm mass abutting the inferior margin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimen is entirely submitted from lateral to medial with one half of the first section in A  the other half in B  etc  through cassette N  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axilla hotspot  1  CT  811  is a 2 x 