ominantly invasive carcinoma  grade 2 of 3  with a papillary architecture and is ER positive  The smaller nodule is located superior and lateral to the larger nodule and is composed of grade 3 of 3 invasive ductal carcinoma with focal spindled morphology and is ER negative  The different morphologies  in combination with the different ER phenotypes  suggest that these tumors represent multicentric disease  rather than multifocal disease  In three of the four positive lymph nodes  the morphology of the tumor cells resembles that of the larger nodule  i e  papillary   The remaining positive lymph node histologically resembles the smaller nodule  The atypical lobular cells are negative for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  WITH MARKED EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The metastatic tumor cells histologically resemble the tumor cells of the smaller nodule  The tumor cells are identified on both hematoxylin and eosin stain and cytokeratin immunohistochemistry  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right axillary lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0 cm firm  tan white lymph node with a tan pink  firm cut surface  A representative section is frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further sections of the lymph node are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right modified axillary radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0 cm specimen consisting of a right mastectomy with attached axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 13 0 cm ellipse of skin attached with an irregularly shaped  REMOVED_DATE x 3 0 cm areol