Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 35 CLINICAL DATA  Poorly differentiated CA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  7 CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 18 OF 18 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a 14 x 16 x 7 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an 11 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  and a 15 x 7 0cm skin ellipse with a nipple in the center  A firm mass is palpable directly below the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 7 x 6 x 6cm relatively well circumscribed tan to yellow nodular mass with focal cystic and soft regions  the largest cyst is 3cm in diameter and contains bloody fluid  The nodular mass grossly abuts against the posterior and inferior resection margin  Four representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A through D  the closest margin  deep  is submitted in A  A representative section of a tan white  fibrous area that extends from the tumor to the inferior resection margin is submitted in cassette E  Similar fibrous tissue on the posterior deep resection margin is submitted in cassette F  which also contains another section of the fibrous tissue  Dissection of the axillary tail yielded multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 3cm to 2 0cm  submitted in cassettes G through L  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
