pared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 97 at 08 44     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in two parts  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number and  breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm fragment of adipose tissue  inked as follows  anterior and posterior black  superior green  medial blue  lateral red  inferior yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  tan  well circumscribed mass present at the lateral and inferior margin and within 0 9cm of the posterior margin  Representative sections are frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen at Cox 5  In addition  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular  ill defined  firm tan white mass with white material oozing from ducts is identified  It is 0 3cm from the superior margin and less than 0 1cm from the anterior margin  Representative sections are submitted as FX 2  now in A  Represen  tative sections of the well circumscribed nodule are submitted in B C  Representative sections of the ill defined mass are submitted in D E  Tissue away from both masses are submitted in F G  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number and  additional medial margin   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm oriented fragment of fibrofatty tissue with two sutures  designated  new medial margin  inked in black with Dr  Smith present  There are multiple firm nodules present in the paren  chyma  The margin is grossly free of tumor  No frozen section is done  Representative sections are submitted in H L  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and designated by Dr  Smith as final medial margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm portion of soft tissue  entirely submitted in M  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  additional infralateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm portion of soft tissue  The lateral surface of the specimen is inked  Cut surface was unremarkable  The specimen was submitted entirely in N Q  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  axillary lymph nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of fat and lymph nodes  The lymph nodes are submitted in R X  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary node tissue   are three fragments of fat and lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm 