Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 93 at 13 55 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  1   OCCUPY A REGION REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  99   INVOLVING DUCTS AND LOBULES THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN AND EXTENDING TO MANY MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 MAY 93 at 12 52                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1  in scant invasive component  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The specimen submitted for BRDU consists primarily of in situ  and scant amounts of invasive carcinoma  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 93 at 16 41     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Estradiol receptor  Negative  Progestin receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick