Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 27 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  SITUATED NEXT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWELVE OF TWELVE LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 36                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy re excision   Received is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm lumpectomy specimen with a small REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm strip of skin  There is a short stitch indicating the superior margin and a long stitch indicating the lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  blue superior margin  red  lateral margin  yellow inferior margin  green medial margin  deep margin black  The specimen is incised to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted in entirety in cassettes A through G  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   Received is a mass of yellow red fatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Dissected are twelve lymph nodes from the axillary pad  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in diameter  The lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes H through J  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   report_end  , Unchecked.
