cal assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in multiple parts  Labeled  wide excision  left breast  and received fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  There is a short stitch and a long stitch designating the superior and the lateral margins resectively  The superior margin is inked in green and lateral in red  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  ill defined nodule  present at 0 2cm from the closest inferior margin  A representative section of the nodule and inferior margin is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  B to D are tumor with additional inferior margins  E to H are sections of superior margin  I and J are sections of the lateral and medial margins submitted en face  Labeled  left axillary contents  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue are multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum dimension and disected from this fatty tissue which is submitted in cassettes K V  Cassettes M V contain half of each lymph node  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fatty tissue  Six lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm and disected from this fatty tissue  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes Q and R  Labeled  additional  superior and deep margin excision  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  No mass is identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes S T and U  Labeled  additional  inferior to deep margin  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  No lesion is identified  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes V and W  Resident  Navneet Narula  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECITON DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRAITING CARCINOMA  MARGINS FREE OF TUMOR  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION PART B  AXILLARY  LEFT   CONTENTS PART C  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY  LEFT   TISSUE PART D  ADDITIONAL DEEP  RE EXCISION PART E  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR TO DEEP MARGIN   report_end  , Unchecked.
