Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 11 01 CLINICAL DATA  NO HISTORY PROVIDED  As per Copath  Status post excisional biopsy of invasive ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 20                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm left simple mastectomy specimen which is oriented with a suture on the 12 0 clock margin  A REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm skin ellipse is present overlying the specimen  with a 6 0cm unremarkable nipple  A 3 5cm well healed linear lunar shaped scar is present on the inferior aspect of the areola  The specimen is black inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy cavity in the inferior aspect at 6 o clock of the specimen  which is 2 0cm from the deep resection margin  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity and the overlying deep margin are submitted in cassette A D  No further masses or lesions are identified  Representative breast parenchyma away from the biopsy cavity is submitted in cassettes E F  No lymph nodes are identified in the lateral portion of the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse excised to a depth of 3 5cm with underlying parenchyma  The specimen is oriented as follows  long suture inferior margin  short sutur