MOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin were performed on three tissue levels of the sentinel lymph node  part B   These immunostains highlight a 0 2cm focus of metastatic carcinoma in the sentinel lymph node  Notably  the focus of metastasis is not present in the permanent H E stained section  The slides for the sentinel lymph node frozen section sample were reviewed in the context of these findings  The focus of metastatic carcinoma is not present on the frozen section slide  Based on this review  the discrepancy between the frozen section sample and final pathology is attributed to sampling  To confirm the diagnosis of invasive carcinoma in the left breast excision  part A   the paraffin blocks for the case were re processed and a panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Although limited by artifact  the stain for calponin and cytokeratin highlight the presence of invasive carcinoma in this section  The stains for myosin and p63 failed and are non contributory  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of oriented breast tissue  with a needle wire localization in place  The long axis is medial to lateral  and the specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green and inferior   yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm ill defined  firm  calcified mass  which is 0 8cm from the medial end margin  2 5cm from the lateral end margin  0 3cm from the anterior margin  0 3cm from the posterior margin  0 6cm from the superior margin and 0 5cm from the inferior margin  The entire specimen is submitted from medial to lateral as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire lumpectomy  from medial to lateral  with the described mass in  REMOVED_ACCES