Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 25 CLINICAL DATA  48 year old female with a right breast lump  Previous 1A  Gr 1  Close margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1   REMOVED_DATE CM SEPARATE FROM THE BIOPSY CAVITY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL LEVEL ONE    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL LEVEL TWO    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN SEVEN OF SEVEN LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 54                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  re excision of right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with two surgical sutures the short stitch indicating the superior margin and the long stitch indicating the lateral margin with an attached ellipse of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Serial sections of the specimen reveal 1 5cm hemorrhagic previous biopsy cavity surrounded by fibrotic tissue  Grossly no evidence of carcinoma is identified  The previous biopsy cavity is located 1 0cm from the superior margin and 0 6cm from the superficial margin  Section code  A  Previous biopsy to superior  B  Previous biopsy to anterior  C D  Previous biopsy to posterior  E  Fibrotic area posterior to lateral  F  Biopsy to skin  G  Biopsy to medial  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel lymph node level one  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fatty lymph node  bisected and entirely submitted in cassettes H and I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel lymph node level two  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of adipose fatty lymph node bisected and entirely submitted in cassette J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibroadipose tiss