ers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a 540 gram  REMOVED_DATE x 15 x 3 2cm left simple mastectomy specimen  On the anterior surface  there is a 9 x 4 5cm portion of skin  consisting of 6cm linear scar with up to 0 5cm of skin excised on either side of it  attached to a REMOVED_DATE x 3cm areolar complex  with 1 x 1 x 0 6cm nipple  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating the axillary tail  Also received in the same container are 2 portions of skin aggregating to 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked blue  and the posterior inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm ill defined firm mass with central fat necrosis and surgical clips  located in the upper outer quadrant of the breast towards the axillary tail  The mass approaches to 0 3cm of the posterior margin  and 2 5cm of the anterior margin  The remainder of the breast is primarily fibroadipose tissue  with small areas of fibrocystic change  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to nearest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nearest anterior margin radially towards mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections through mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of fibrocystic change adjacent to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of apparently unremarkable fibroadipose tissue distant from mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section through scar on skin  and representative sections through also separately submitted skin in same container  Received in formalin  labeled  additional inferior tissue  left breast   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to 5 x 4 x 0 8cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 27   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 02 18PM By his her signature above  the path