t with tumor bed       BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION   MICROSCOPIC FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS AND FOCAL COLUMNAR CELL CHANGE   SCLEROSING ADENOSIS   SEE NOTE    NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains  cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam REMOVED_DATE  calponin  myosin  and p63  do not demonstrate a myoepithelial cells lining around the foci of  carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional markers to better characterize these foci of  carcinoma are in progress and will be reported separately       BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR   EXCISION   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS       BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL   EXCISION   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU    FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  RADIAL SCAR  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS   INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA   SEE NOTE    NOTE  The lobular neoplasia cells are negative for E cadherin by  immunohistochemistry   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID         BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN LATERAL   EXCISION   FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY       GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received are 5 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME    REMOVE_MRN     Received fresh  labeled  left breast lumpectomy  stitch short superior  long  lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm lumpectomy specimen  oriented as follows   Short stitch   superior  long stitch   lateral  There is a needle localization  guide wire within the specimen  The long axis of the specimen is the  anterior posterior axis  and the specimen is inked as follows  Superior    blue  inferior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is  serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a 5 x 3 x 2 5cm area  of tan white fibrous tissue in the anterior region of the specimen  located REMOVED_DATE  cm to the anterior margin  abutting the superior and medial margins  located 1  cm to the inferior margin  1 5cm to the lateral margin  and 4cm to the  posterior tip  A metal clip is identified in this area  and is located 1 4cm  from the superior margin  1 3cm from the medial margin  1 8cm from the  inferior margin  3 3cm from the lateral margin  2 8cm from the anterior tip   and 4 5cm from the posterior tip  No masses are identified  The remainder of  the specimen consists of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is  submitted as follows     SECTION CODE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior tip  en face    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior tip  en face    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue anterior to clip    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue immediately anterior to clip    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area where clip was identified  including clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibrous tissue immediately posterior to clip    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibroadipose tissue away from the area of  fibrous tissue  from the posterior region of the specimen     Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin superior   are 3  unoriented fragments of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x  2 8 x 1 1cm  which are serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or  abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin inferior   are 4  unoriented fragments of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x  2 9 x 0 8cm  which are serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or  abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin medial   are 2  unoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm   which are serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or abnormalities  The  specimen